From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iosub <iosub@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 28 Nov 2025 18:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix multimodal embd_size calculation for vision models

Fixes GGML_ASSERT failure when generating with multimodal models that
have vision projectors (e.g., qwen3vl, mllama). The embd_size buffer
was calculated using only the text model's n_embd, not accounting for
the additional embedding dimensions from vision projectors.

This caused buffer overflow when both text and vision embeddings needed
to be stored during generation, resulting in:
  GGML_ASSERT((n_outputs_prev + n_outputs)*n_embd <= embd_size) failed

Solution: Use maximum embedding dimension between text and vision when
calculating buffer size for multimodal models.
---
 src/llama-context.cpp | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 7d77f0732..8a9c7b42e 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -1306,7 +1306,16 @@ uint32_t llama_context::output_reserve(uint32_t n_outputs_max) {
     }
 
     logits_size = has_logits ? n_vocab*n_outputs_max : 0;
-    embd_size   = has_embd   ?  n_embd*n_outputs_max : 0;
+    
+    // For multimodal models with vision projectors, we need to account for
+    // the larger embedding dimension. Vision projectors (e.g., qwen3vl's
+    // qwen3vl_merger) may have different n_embd than the text model.
+    // Use n_embd_inp which represents the maximum input embedding dimension.
+    uint32_t n_embd_total = n_embd;
+    if (model.hparams.n_embd_inp() > n_embd) {
+        n_embd_total = model.hparams.n_embd_inp();
+    }
+    embd_size   = has_embd   ?  n_embd_total*n_outputs_max : 0;
 
     if (output_ids.empty()) {
         // init, never resized afterwards
